# .npmrc — pnpm notes for the Noujoude Digital Heritage Museum (Phase 0/1)
#
# STATUS AS MEASURED 1 NOVEMBER 2026, AFTER OWNER DECISIONS OD-7 AND OD-2 WERE EXECUTED. The whole
# body below is the measurement record and is kept verbatim; these lines state what is now true:
#   • OD-7 IS ARMED. `pnpm config set verify-deps-before-run error --global` was run, and the value
#     is live in pnpm 11.21.0's global config file — `C:\Users\NaDa\AppData\Local\pnpm\config\config.yaml`
#     (`verifyDepsBeforeRun: error`), which is lever 1 working exactly as measured below. Verified by
#     `pnpm config get --global verify-deps-before-run` → `error`, and by `pnpm run audit:workflow`
#     exiting 0 with zero `Progress:` lines emitted.
#   • THE TRAP'S TRIGGER IS GONE ANYWAY. OD-2 installed the tree, so `node_modules` now exists and the
#     missing-dependency path that started the install cannot be reached. `scripts/preflight.mjs`
#     check 10 reports PASS from the tree and still prints the global value, so the guard stays visible.
#   • UNRELATED MACHINE CONFIG WAS PRESERVED. The three keys that were already in that file
#     (fetchRetries, fetchTimeout, networkConcurrency) are untouched; the pre-change file is backed up.
#   • THE LINE-BY-LINE MEASUREMENTS BELOW STILL HOLD for any machine where OD-7 has NOT been applied —
#     which is why they are not deleted. On such a machine, everything below is still current advice.
#
# THIS FILE INTENTIONALLY SETS NO OPTIONS. Every candidate was measured against the pnpm actually
# installed here (11.21.0, corepack at `C:\Users\NaDa\AppData\Local\node\corepack\v1\pnpm\11.21.0`)
# and each one either does nothing or does not fix the problem it was considered for. A settings file
# that looks like a guard and is not one is the defect class holes H-9, H-10 and H-11 were all about.
#
# THE PROBLEM (measured 1 November 2026, recorded as docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md §8 hole H-12).
# `pnpm run <script>` in this workspace does not run the script. pnpm first checks whether the
# dependencies declared in `package.json` exist, and because `node_modules` is absent **by design**
# (blocker B-02, gated behind Owner decision OD-2), it starts `pnpm install` before the script:
#
#     $ pnpm run audit:workflow
#     [WARN] Unsupported engine: wanted: {"node":">=24.22.1 <25"} (current: {"node":"v24.19.0",…
#     Progress: resolved 1, reused 0, downloaded 0, added 0
#     … Progress: resolved 669 …              ← network resolution of the whole tree
#
# The command was issued as a read-only documentation gate and became a dependency install. It was
# killed. The workspace gained nothing — no `node_modules`, no `pnpm-lock.yaml` were created — but
# packages were written to the machine-level content-addressable store at `E:\.pnpm-store\v11`
# (`pnpm store path`, directory mtime 1 Nov 2026 07:23), which is outside this project and outside
# this batch's authority to clean.
#
# WHY THE OBVIOUS FIXES DO NOT WORK HERE — each tested, not reasoned about from documentation:
#
#   • `verify-deps-before-run=error` in THIS file → **ignored**. `verify-deps-before-run` is one of
#     the 67 keys pnpm 11.21.0 reads only from the *global* pnpm config file (its `pnpmConfigFileKeys`
#     list, in `dist/pnpm.mjs`). Proved two ways: the run above still installed with this line
#     present, and a control line `registry=https://registry.example.invalid/` placed in this same
#     file *was* honoured (`GET https://registry.example.invalid/… ENOTFOUND`), so the file is read —
#     only this key is not.
#   • `pnpm run --no-verify-deps-before-run <script>` and `pnpm --no-… run <script>` →
#     `[ERROR] Unknown option: 'verify-deps-before-run'`, exit 1. No CLI form exists.
#   • `engine-strict=true` (a key this file CAN set) → does not help: the deps check runs first, so
#     the engine complaint stayed a WARN and the install still started. Removed after the test.
#   • `pnpm config get verify-deps-before-run` → `undefined`, and there is no `~/.npmrc` and no
#     `%LOCALAPPDATA%\pnpm\config\rc` on this host: the built-in default `install` is in force.
#
# WHAT DOES WORK — the two effective levers, both machine-level and therefore Owner decisions, not
# something this batch may do:
#
#   1. Global, once per machine:       pnpm config set verify-deps-before-run error --global
#   2. Per shell, no machine change:    pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run=error pnpm run <script>
#      measured: fails in about two seconds with `[ERR_PNPM_VERIFY_DEPS_BEFORE_RUN] Cannot check
#      whether dependencies are outdated / Run "pnpm install"`, exit 1, nothing resolved, nothing
#      downloaded.
#
# EVERY VALUE MEASURED, 1 Nov 2026, so that "arm the guard" is not a guess about which value does what.
# Each value was set through lever 2 in a temp fixture holding a declared dependency, no `node_modules`,
# no lockfile, stdin closed — and a project `.npmrc` pointing the registry at
# `https://registry.example.invalid/`, which lever ① above proves this file CAN set: a value that still
# starts an install therefore dies on ENOTFOUND instead of writing into the machine store. Nothing was
# added to the workspace or to the store by these runs (no lockfile, no `node_modules` afterwards).
#
#   install / unset  registry resolution begins before the script is reached — the trap, as measured
#   error            exit 1, ERR_PNPM_VERIFY_DEPS_BEFORE_RUN. Refuses. Nothing resolved or downloaded.
#   warn             exit 0, `[WARN] Your node_modules are out of sync …` and THEN THE SCRIPT RUNS.
#   prompt           exit 1 here only because stdin was not a terminal; pnpm's prompt defaults to yes,
#                    so at a keyboard this value is one Enter away from the install. Not a guard.
#   false            exit 0, script runs, no notice, nothing fetched.
#   anything else    exit 0, script runs, nothing fetched — `runDepsStatusCheck`'s switch covers
#                    install/prompt/error/warn and has NO default case, so junk falls through. Safe by
#                    accident, not by design, and a version bump could take the accident away.
#
# So lever 1 with `error` is the only setting that cannot install, and `scripts/preflight.mjs` check 10
# classifies the values exactly this way rather than treating any non-`install` string as guarded.
#
# UNTIL ONE OF THOSE IS SET, the safe way to execute this repository's own checks is the underlying
# command rather than the `pnpm` alias — `node scripts/verify-citations.mjs`, `node scripts/preflight.mjs`,
# `node scripts/tests/<suite>.test.mjs` — which is what `docs/TEST_AND_RELEASE_REPORT.md` §9 prints.
# `scripts/preflight.mjs` now reports the state of this trap as its own check, so the next engineer is
# told before they are surprised.
#
# This file must never hold credentials: `.gitignore` does not exclude `.npmrc`, so anything written
# here is committed the moment the repository exists (B-04, OD-4).
